1
00:00:02,600 --> 00:00:06,000
National Radio and Television Administration.

2
00:01:25,000 --> 00:01:30,000
Welcome to Sister Pang's Bathhouse.

3
00:01:37,759 --> 00:01:39,440
Nuannuan, come eat some meat.

4
00:01:40,960 --> 00:01:41,890
It's delicious.

5
00:01:42,440 --> 00:01:43,440
Auntie, look.

6
00:01:43,440 --> 00:01:44,920
This is Mom and Dad.

7
00:01:44,920 --> 00:01:46,479
This is you and Uncle.

8
00:01:46,560 --> 00:01:49,039
And the one in the middle is me.

9
00:01:49,840 --> 00:01:50,680
Awesome.

10
00:01:50,680 --> 00:01:52,560
You draw so well, Nuannuan.

11
00:01:52,560 --> 00:01:54,560
This drawing is quite creative.

12
00:01:54,680 --> 00:01:56,400
She made you look quite handsome.

13
00:01:56,400 --> 00:01:57,039
Really?

14
00:01:57,320 --> 00:01:59,479
Of course. Uncle is very handsome.

15
00:01:59,479 --> 00:02:00,560
Even more handsome than Dad.

16
00:02:00,560 --> 00:02:02,760
Let me see who is more handsome than Dad.

17
00:02:02,920 --> 00:02:04,440
Children have sharp eyes.

18
00:02:06,120 --> 00:02:08,560
Nuannuan's drawing is even better than last time.

19
00:02:08,560 --> 00:02:09,840
She really has a lot of talent.

20
00:02:09,840 --> 00:02:10,440
Nuannuan,

21
00:02:10,600 --> 00:02:12,560
how about Mommy finds you an art teacher?

22
00:02:12,560 --> 00:02:13,400
You can become

23
00:02:13,400 --> 00:02:15,660
a very, very great painter in the future.

24
00:02:18,240 --> 00:02:20,640
Becoming a great painter is not important.

25
00:02:20,720 --> 00:02:21,760
As long as Nuannuan is happy.

26
00:02:21,760 --> 00:02:22,800
We can draw if we want to,

27
00:02:22,800 --> 00:02:24,079
and not draw if we don't want to.

28
00:02:24,079 --> 00:02:24,480
Right? Right.

29
00:02:24,480 --> 00:02:25,079
Cheng Fei.

30
00:02:25,079 --> 00:02:26,410
Yes, Nuannuan is right.

31
00:02:26,640 --> 00:02:30,040
The most important thing is for the family to be happy, right?

32
00:02:30,800 --> 00:02:32,079
Shall we make a toast?

33
00:02:32,079 --> 00:02:35,360
Cheers. Being happy is the most important thing.

34
00:02:36,840 --> 00:02:38,840
Can we come out and play more often?

35
00:02:38,840 --> 00:02:40,000
Of course we can.

36
00:02:45,680 --> 00:02:46,440
What does Nuannuan want to eat?

37
00:02:46,440 --> 00:02:47,840
Daddy will get it for you.

38
00:02:48,280 --> 00:02:49,040
I want to eat that.

39
00:02:49,040 --> 00:02:50,040
That one? Okay.

40
00:03:27,600 --> 00:03:31,160
How did I do as a cardboard cutout today?

41
00:03:32,880 --> 00:03:34,880
What do you mean, cardboard cutout?

42
00:03:36,200 --> 00:03:38,400
I just wanted to hang out with you.

43
00:03:38,600 --> 00:03:40,120
You're so paranoid.

44
00:03:40,200 --> 00:03:41,130
What's going on?

45
00:03:44,160 --> 00:03:46,480
They're having relationship problems, aren't they?

46
00:03:46,480 --> 00:03:47,400
How bad is it?

47
00:03:50,400 --> 00:03:51,840
There's no proof of that.

48
00:03:51,840 --> 00:03:53,640
Why are you making wild guesses?

49
00:03:53,800 --> 00:03:55,320
Just tell me, did you have fun?

50
00:03:55,320 --> 00:03:56,180
Were you happy?

51
00:03:56,200 --> 00:03:57,880
Did you enjoy the barbecue?

52
00:03:58,400 --> 00:03:59,120
I had fun.

53
00:03:59,400 --> 00:04:00,120
I was happy.

54
00:04:00,200 --> 00:04:01,520
The meat was delicious too.

55
00:04:01,520 --> 00:04:03,320
Bring your uncle out more often.

56
00:04:04,600 --> 00:04:07,040
What, are you addicted?

57
00:04:08,000 --> 00:04:10,040
Kids have no filter.

58
00:04:10,040 --> 00:04:11,320
Are you a kid too?

59
00:04:12,640 --> 00:04:14,040
Just focus on driving.

60
00:04:14,760 --> 00:04:16,089
What are you looking at?

61
00:04:17,480 --> 00:04:19,399
Well, I'm gonna take a quick nap.

62
00:04:20,040 --> 00:04:20,700
I'm sleepy.

63
00:04:44,600 --> 00:04:45,320
Master.

64
00:04:45,720 --> 00:04:46,440
This lumbar cushion

65
00:04:46,440 --> 00:04:48,600
can support your lower back

66
00:04:48,720 --> 00:04:50,180
and relieve the pressure.

67
00:04:50,200 --> 00:04:50,760
Try it.

68
00:04:51,120 --> 00:04:51,720
Thank you.

69
00:04:51,880 --> 00:04:54,320
But I'm not really used to it.

70
00:04:54,600 --> 00:04:56,040
Then you should definitely try it.

71
00:04:56,040 --> 00:04:57,320
You'll get used to it.

72
00:04:57,320 --> 00:04:58,920
Trust me, you can't go wrong.

73
00:04:59,720 --> 00:05:00,650
Okay, thank you.

74
00:05:01,880 --> 00:05:02,640
Master,

75
00:05:03,760 --> 00:05:06,160
how did you hurt your lower back?

76
00:05:08,920 --> 00:05:10,440
I spoke out of turn. Sorry.

77
00:05:11,080 --> 00:05:12,440
You should take care of your health

78
00:05:12,440 --> 00:05:13,440
and strike a balance between work and rest.

79
00:05:13,440 --> 00:05:14,240
I'm going out.

80
00:05:19,560 --> 00:05:21,560
I don't know what's wrong with my back lately.

81
00:05:21,560 --> 00:05:22,560
It hurts so much.

82
00:05:24,440 --> 00:05:25,000
Chao.

83
00:05:25,320 --> 00:05:27,040
Rub it for me. Come on.

84
00:05:28,040 --> 00:05:28,880
It hurts.

85
00:05:30,160 --> 00:05:31,490
Does your back hurt too?

86
00:05:32,320 --> 00:05:33,280
That lumbar cushion works really well.

87
00:05:33,280 --> 00:05:34,440
I'll send you a link.

88
00:05:37,480 --> 00:05:38,240
Thank you.

89
00:05:38,600 --> 00:05:40,600
Bowen, I know an old Chinese medicine doctor.

90
00:05:40,600 --> 00:05:41,840
It's awesome.

91
00:05:42,080 --> 00:05:43,920
Do you want me to push it over to you?

92
00:05:43,920 --> 00:05:44,760
No need.

93
00:05:45,320 --> 00:05:46,720
You massage really well.

94
00:06:15,120 --> 00:06:16,320
Hello, Jia'er.

95
00:06:16,320 --> 00:06:17,320
How have you been lately?

96
00:06:17,320 --> 00:06:17,800
Well,

97
00:06:17,800 --> 00:06:20,000
could you recommend a marriage counseling service to me?

98
00:06:20,000 --> 00:06:20,800
I want to give it a try.

99
00:06:20,800 --> 00:06:22,400
I'll find some professional ones later

100
00:06:22,400 --> 00:06:23,320
and send them to you.

101
00:06:23,320 --> 00:06:24,320
They should be able to help you.

102
00:06:24,320 --> 00:06:25,080
Thanks.

103
00:06:26,480 --> 00:06:27,560
I plan to ask the company

104
00:06:27,560 --> 00:06:29,120
for all the annual leave

105
00:06:29,120 --> 00:06:30,800
I haven't taken in the past two years.

106
00:06:30,800 --> 00:06:32,680
Besides this marriage counseling,

107
00:06:32,680 --> 00:06:35,240
I also want to take them on a trip to Iceland.

108
00:06:35,240 --> 00:06:35,960
Yeah,

109
00:06:36,320 --> 00:06:37,400
you do need to relax

110
00:06:37,400 --> 00:06:38,680
and get a change of scenery.

111
00:06:38,680 --> 00:06:40,159
That's it for now. Bye.

112
00:06:46,440 --> 00:06:47,200
Come on.

113
00:06:47,880 --> 00:06:49,440
We're home.

114
00:06:51,360 --> 00:06:52,890
What do you want for dinner?

115
00:06:53,440 --> 00:06:54,560
Anything is fine.

116
00:06:56,560 --> 00:06:58,290
Playing as soon as you get back.

117
00:06:58,560 --> 00:07:01,000
Your mom will definitely scold you if she sees you.

118
00:07:01,000 --> 00:07:02,680
Dad, don't worry.

119
00:07:02,800 --> 00:07:05,560
Mom never comes back before dark.

120
00:07:05,640 --> 00:07:08,880
She's always busy, busy, busy.

121
00:07:08,880 --> 00:07:10,200
You smart little thing.

122
00:07:10,200 --> 00:07:11,200
Drink your water.

123
00:07:15,160 --> 00:07:16,290
You're early today.

124
00:07:18,320 --> 00:07:20,080
I took annual leave from work.

125
00:07:21,560 --> 00:07:22,320
Nuannuan,

126
00:07:23,240 --> 00:07:25,440
how about Dad and I take you out to play?

127
00:07:25,440 --> 00:07:26,320
Really?

128
00:07:26,320 --> 00:07:26,880
Yes, really.

129
00:07:26,880 --> 00:07:29,760
Let's take some time off school and go out to play, okay?

130
00:07:29,760 --> 00:07:30,760
Awesome!

131
00:07:32,560 --> 00:07:35,960
Why are you playing on the tablet again as soon as you get back?

132
00:07:37,800 --> 00:07:38,600
Then you can

133
00:07:39,400 --> 00:07:40,480
play for another fifteen minutes.

134
00:07:40,480 --> 00:07:41,240
Okay.

135
00:07:43,760 --> 00:07:45,880
Haven't you always wanted to go to Iceland?

136
00:07:45,880 --> 00:07:48,200
I just finalized things with the travel agency today.

137
00:07:48,200 --> 00:07:49,240
We'll leave in a week.

138
00:07:49,240 --> 00:07:50,000
First, we'll go to Iceland.

139
00:07:50,000 --> 00:07:51,000
We'll stay there for a week.

140
00:07:51,000 --> 00:07:52,720
Then we'll head to Norway.

141
00:07:52,720 --> 00:07:54,000
After four days in Norway,

142
00:07:54,000 --> 00:07:55,560
we'll spend two days in Finland.

143
00:07:55,560 --> 00:07:57,159
And in Finland, we'll take...

144
00:07:57,159 --> 00:07:58,240
Zhao Jia.

145
00:08:00,320 --> 00:08:02,240
There's something I want to tell you.

146
00:08:02,240 --> 00:08:02,770
Go ahead.

147
00:08:05,560 --> 00:08:06,760
Let me take this call.

148
00:08:08,760 --> 00:08:09,240
Hello?

149
00:08:09,800 --> 00:08:10,240
Hello.

150
00:08:10,360 --> 00:08:11,360
Is this Zhao Jia?

151
00:08:11,560 --> 00:08:12,220
Who is this?

152
00:08:12,320 --> 00:08:14,320
I'm calling from the Anping District People's Court.

153
00:08:14,320 --> 00:08:15,800
Your husband, Cheng Fei, just filed

154
00:08:15,800 --> 00:08:17,130
a petition for divorce.

155
00:08:17,400 --> 00:08:18,600
According to the law,

156
00:08:18,600 --> 00:08:20,920
we need to arrange a pre-litigation mediation.

157
00:08:20,920 --> 00:08:22,850
I'd like to check the time with you.

158
00:08:29,400 --> 00:08:30,200
What did I say?

159
00:08:30,400 --> 00:08:31,960
Didn't I say it was a big client?

160
00:08:31,960 --> 00:08:33,220
Am I sensitive or what?

161
00:08:33,320 --> 00:08:33,960
I'm telling you, sometimes

162
00:08:33,960 --> 00:08:35,640
I even suspect I have some kind of sixth sense.

163
00:08:35,640 --> 00:08:36,200
Still want to argue?

164
00:08:36,200 --> 00:08:37,080
No more arguing.

165
00:08:37,080 --> 00:08:37,880
You win.

166
00:08:38,080 --> 00:08:39,840
Our opponent this time is Lawyer Li again.

167
00:08:39,840 --> 00:08:41,080
Then we're bound to win.

168
00:08:41,080 --> 00:08:42,679
That suitcase doesn't understand human nature at all.

169
00:08:42,679 --> 00:08:43,640
When it comes to emotions,

170
00:08:43,640 --> 00:08:44,440
he's way behind.

171
00:08:44,440 --> 00:08:45,840
Way behind who?

172
00:08:45,840 --> 00:08:46,640
Me, of course.

173
00:08:46,840 --> 00:08:49,160
Then, relationship expert, analyze this for us.

174
00:08:49,160 --> 00:08:51,200
Why is Cheng Fei so determined to get a divorce?

175
00:08:51,200 --> 00:08:52,960
That's so simple.

176
00:08:52,960 --> 00:08:53,880
Think about it.

177
00:08:53,960 --> 00:08:56,200
If a man is so determined to get a divorce,

178
00:08:56,200 --> 00:08:57,800
he definitely has someone else lined up.

179
00:08:57,800 --> 00:08:59,400
Otherwise, he wouldn't be so motivated.

180
00:08:59,400 --> 00:09:00,600
I've seen this kind of thing a lot.

181
00:09:00,600 --> 00:09:02,760
No, you have to look on the bright side.

182
00:09:02,760 --> 00:09:04,160
Maybe he has a terminal illness

183
00:09:04,160 --> 00:09:05,960
and doesn't want to burden his wife and child.

184
00:09:05,960 --> 00:09:06,520
Miao,

185
00:09:06,520 --> 00:09:07,780
watch fewer TV dramas.

186
00:09:08,160 --> 00:09:10,160
It's also possible that, like Gauguin,

187
00:09:10,160 --> 00:09:11,640
he suddenly went to find himself.

188
00:09:11,640 --> 00:09:12,400
Makes sense.

189
00:09:12,960 --> 00:09:13,880
Who is Gauguin?

190
00:09:14,440 --> 00:09:15,440
A painter.

191
00:09:16,160 --> 00:09:18,220
'The Moon and Sixpence' is about him.

192
00:09:18,600 --> 00:09:19,160
This... this...

193
00:09:19,160 --> 00:09:20,840
I've read this Sixpence thing.

194
00:09:20,840 --> 00:09:21,760
Isn't it in the same series

195
00:09:21,760 --> 00:09:22,840
as Grimm's Fairy Tales?

196
00:09:22,840 --> 00:09:24,240
Written by Grimm, right?

197
00:09:24,960 --> 00:09:25,640
Right?

198
00:09:25,880 --> 00:09:26,720
Alright.

199
00:09:26,920 --> 00:09:29,640
Since we don't understand, let's figure it out.

200
00:09:30,200 --> 00:09:30,930
Understood.

201
00:09:35,400 --> 00:09:36,400
Let's go. What are you doing?

202
00:09:36,400 --> 00:09:37,720
Let's go investigate.

203
00:09:38,920 --> 00:09:39,640
Let's go.

204
00:09:40,520 --> 00:09:41,640
Say something, Uncle.

205
00:09:41,640 --> 00:09:42,880
No, just think about it.

206
00:09:42,880 --> 00:09:43,880
What could this mean?

207
00:09:43,880 --> 00:09:45,010
I... I didn't see it.

208
00:09:52,200 --> 00:09:52,840
How is it?

209
00:09:53,520 --> 00:09:56,050
Much better, but it still seems a bit swollen.

210
00:10:15,640 --> 00:10:16,500
Take a picture.

211
00:10:24,560 --> 00:10:25,640
Did you have fun today?

212
00:10:25,640 --> 00:10:26,400
Yes.

213
00:10:26,400 --> 00:10:27,520
I had an art class.

214
00:10:29,880 --> 00:10:32,340
Did the teacher tell you to drink more water?

215
00:10:34,120 --> 00:10:34,850
How did it go?

216
00:10:34,880 --> 00:10:36,140
Did you find anything?

217
00:10:36,720 --> 00:10:39,250
I found that Cheng Fei is indeed a good doctor.

218
00:10:39,440 --> 00:10:40,640
And a good father too.

219
00:10:41,440 --> 00:10:44,000
Why did such a good man have to get a divorce?

220
00:10:44,120 --> 00:10:44,920
I don't get it.

221
00:10:47,040 --> 00:10:47,560
Uncle.

222
00:10:48,000 --> 00:10:49,080
Li, Li, Li...

223
00:10:49,480 --> 00:10:50,600
Lawyer Li is here.

224
00:10:50,600 --> 00:10:51,840
So what if he's here? Why are you yelling?

225
00:10:51,840 --> 00:10:52,720
Are you crazy?

226
00:10:52,720 --> 00:10:54,720
Cheng Fei is starting to touch Li Lv.

227
00:11:06,960 --> 00:11:08,420
What's going on with them?

228
00:11:15,360 --> 00:11:17,360
For your previously injured area,

229
00:11:18,240 --> 00:11:20,240
you need to do more strength training.

230
00:11:20,240 --> 00:11:20,720
You're always like this.

231
00:11:20,720 --> 00:11:22,720
How can you be okay if it never heals?

232
00:11:22,720 --> 00:11:23,520
It's been so many years.

233
00:11:23,520 --> 00:11:24,650
It's an old problem.

234
00:11:24,960 --> 00:11:26,360
You have to do McKenzie exercises every day.

235
00:11:26,360 --> 00:11:27,240
Do ten sets.

236
00:11:38,360 --> 00:11:39,840
Stop working. Let's eat.

237
00:11:41,000 --> 00:11:43,000
You go ahead. I'll work a bit longer.

238
00:11:46,360 --> 00:11:48,290
That suitcase was damaged before.

239
00:11:49,480 --> 00:11:50,410
How did you know?

240
00:11:50,720 --> 00:11:53,180
I went to Cheng Fei's and saw him doing rehab.

241
00:11:54,320 --> 00:11:55,580
How did he get injured?

242
00:11:55,760 --> 00:11:57,290
It happened a long time ago.

243
00:11:58,080 --> 00:11:59,680
Why do you care so much about him?

244
00:11:59,680 --> 00:12:00,600
Just curious.

245
00:12:00,800 --> 00:12:02,080
Ask him if you're so curious.

246
00:12:02,080 --> 00:12:03,440
Why would I ask him?

247
00:12:09,960 --> 00:12:12,400
Then let me ask you a personal question.

248
00:12:16,440 --> 00:12:17,200
Ask away.

249
00:12:19,600 --> 00:12:21,400
What's going on between you two?

250
00:12:23,040 --> 00:12:24,680
That's way too personal.

251
00:12:24,680 --> 00:12:27,680
We're just chatting. What's the big deal? We're bros.

252
00:12:31,800 --> 00:12:33,560
Like I care. You two...

253
00:12:35,440 --> 00:12:35,680
What's going on?

254
00:12:35,680 --> 00:12:37,540
Come here and take a look. Come on.

255
00:12:44,560 --> 00:12:46,320
Look. Look at those eyes.

256
00:12:47,040 --> 00:12:48,040
Look at this hand.

257
00:12:49,560 --> 00:12:51,080
Am I being too sensitive?

258
00:12:51,680 --> 00:12:52,400
No.

259
00:12:53,200 --> 00:12:55,060
Actually, it's understandable.

260
00:12:58,600 --> 00:13:00,320
Human emotions are fluid.

261
00:13:08,560 --> 00:13:10,560
Why is he acting so weird lately?

262
00:13:31,560 --> 00:13:33,080
These are the new short-sleeved shirts in our store.

263
00:13:33,080 --> 00:13:34,480
They are all 100% cotton.

264
00:13:35,080 --> 00:13:36,960
Do you have this in a hardshell?

265
00:13:36,960 --> 00:13:38,320
Like, with better quality.

266
00:13:38,320 --> 00:13:40,120
Then let's take a look over here.

267
00:13:40,200 --> 00:13:41,920
He can wear it as casual clothes for commuting.

268
00:13:41,920 --> 00:13:43,440
It depends on what your boyfriend needs.

269
00:13:43,440 --> 00:13:45,440
Usually, he wears white to work.

270
00:13:46,080 --> 00:13:47,080
I'll take this one.

271
00:13:47,080 --> 00:13:47,920
Okay.

272
00:13:49,920 --> 00:13:51,160
Let me confirm one last time

273
00:13:51,160 --> 00:13:53,200
if there is any room for compromise between both parties.

274
00:13:53,200 --> 00:13:53,840
No.

275
00:13:54,240 --> 00:13:54,920
No.

276
00:13:55,160 --> 00:13:56,960
Due to the intense conflict between both parties,

277
00:13:56,960 --> 00:13:58,440
this court will no longer mediate

278
00:13:58,440 --> 00:14:00,570
and will proceed to the trial process.

279
00:14:06,800 --> 00:14:07,600
Cheng Fei.

280
00:14:10,240 --> 00:14:12,300
You have so many complaints about me.

281
00:14:12,440 --> 00:14:14,280
Why didn't you usually communicate with me?

282
00:14:14,280 --> 00:14:15,280
What's the point?

283
00:14:15,440 --> 00:14:17,370
Neither of us can change the other.

284
00:14:18,720 --> 00:14:20,180
Stop making a scene, okay?

285
00:14:20,200 --> 00:14:22,920
Let's go home. We can solve the problems, okay?

286
00:14:23,680 --> 00:14:24,960
We are no longer suited

287
00:14:24,960 --> 00:14:26,440
to live together.

288
00:14:29,520 --> 00:14:31,400
More than ten years together.

289
00:14:31,960 --> 00:14:33,400
You just say we're not suited and that's it?

290
00:14:33,400 --> 00:14:35,040
Have you ever respected me?

291
00:14:35,440 --> 00:14:36,680
Let's not talk about it here.

292
00:14:36,680 --> 00:14:37,920
It's embarrassing for everyone.

293
00:14:37,920 --> 00:14:39,320
Who is embarrassing who now?

294
00:14:39,320 --> 00:14:41,650
You're the one insisting on this divorce.

295
00:14:41,800 --> 00:14:43,320
More than ten years.

296
00:14:43,840 --> 00:14:46,600
Can you just say you don't want this anymore?

297
00:14:46,600 --> 00:14:48,680
Why do I find that so hard to believe, Cheng Fei?

298
00:14:48,680 --> 00:14:50,680
Cheng Fei, tell me. What did I do wrong?

299
00:14:50,680 --> 00:14:52,560
Why do you insist on a divorce?

300
00:14:52,720 --> 00:14:53,320
Cheng Fei.

301
00:14:57,560 --> 00:14:58,720
Just tell the truth.

302
00:15:06,720 --> 00:15:08,520
I fell in love with someone else.

303
00:15:10,280 --> 00:15:12,400
I think she can give me the life I want.

304
00:15:13,920 --> 00:15:15,780
But we are just friends right now.

305
00:15:15,960 --> 00:15:18,290
I want to sort out our relationship first.

306
00:15:25,960 --> 00:15:27,890
You fell in love with someone else.

307
00:15:30,600 --> 00:15:32,960
You should have told me earlier if you fell in love with someone else.

308
00:15:32,960 --> 00:15:33,560
If you had told me earlier,

309
00:15:33,560 --> 00:15:35,290
I would have let you go earlier.

310
00:15:36,720 --> 00:15:37,680
Why are you pretending?

311
00:15:37,680 --> 00:15:38,440
Zhao Jia.

312
00:15:39,080 --> 00:15:40,280
Except for Nuannuan,

313
00:15:41,560 --> 00:15:42,960
I don't want anything else.

314
00:15:42,960 --> 00:15:43,890
As for Nuannuan,

315
00:15:45,520 --> 00:15:48,050
you will never take her away in this lifetime.

316
00:16:00,240 --> 00:16:02,900
You should have told Zhao Jia the truth earlier.

317
00:16:03,160 --> 00:16:04,640
I didn't want to upset her.

318
00:16:06,360 --> 00:16:08,240
Our divorce is between us.

319
00:16:08,240 --> 00:16:10,300
It has nothing to do with anyone else.

320
00:16:11,000 --> 00:16:13,520
But the moment you had someone else in your heart,

321
00:16:13,520 --> 00:16:15,000
hurt was inevitable.

322
00:16:23,480 --> 00:16:25,120
I searched the whole house.

323
00:16:25,120 --> 00:16:27,780
But I just couldn't find that divorce judgment.

324
00:16:28,160 --> 00:16:29,520
The court doesn't have it either.

325
00:16:29,520 --> 00:16:30,980
They didn't keep a record.

326
00:16:31,480 --> 00:16:33,240
Is there any other way?

327
00:16:34,880 --> 00:16:36,280
Ask my ex-husband for it.

328
00:16:36,880 --> 00:16:38,160
Oh my God.

329
00:16:38,480 --> 00:16:39,400
This...

330
00:16:43,240 --> 00:16:44,120
Okay.

331
00:16:44,160 --> 00:16:45,040
Alright.

332
00:16:47,880 --> 00:16:48,640
Bad news.

333
00:16:49,280 --> 00:16:50,540
Son, did you hear that?

334
00:16:50,640 --> 00:16:53,680
I heard you. Ask your ex-husband for the divorce decree.

335
00:16:53,680 --> 00:16:55,410
Where's my bottle opener, Mom?

336
00:16:55,520 --> 00:16:56,650
In the first drawer.

337
00:16:59,400 --> 00:17:00,120
Son.

338
00:17:01,760 --> 00:17:02,480
Son.

339
00:17:04,160 --> 00:17:04,890
Have a peach.

340
00:17:06,280 --> 00:17:07,740
Here's what I'm thinking.

341
00:17:07,760 --> 00:17:10,160
If Li Guochen and I meet,

342
00:17:10,520 --> 00:17:12,319
it'll definitely be a disaster.

343
00:17:13,240 --> 00:17:14,160
Look.

344
00:17:14,160 --> 00:17:16,760
Can you help me talk to him about this?

345
00:17:17,000 --> 00:17:19,000
No, Mom. This is between the two of you.

346
00:17:19,000 --> 00:17:19,640
It's better if you

347
00:17:19,640 --> 00:17:20,970
communicate directly.

348
00:17:21,760 --> 00:17:22,359
Son.

349
00:17:22,359 --> 00:17:24,520
I know this is a hassle for you.

350
00:17:24,640 --> 00:17:26,160
But please help me out.

351
00:17:45,560 --> 00:17:47,920
Are you not busy at work today?

352
00:17:48,000 --> 00:17:49,520
It's okay. Not too busy.

353
00:17:55,640 --> 00:17:56,640
What's up?

354
00:18:00,760 --> 00:18:01,880
My mom is back.

355
00:18:04,880 --> 00:18:06,000
Doesn't your mom

356
00:18:07,000 --> 00:18:09,160
come back every year or two?

357
00:18:10,240 --> 00:18:10,920
Yes.

358
00:18:11,240 --> 00:18:14,640
But this time I need a favor from you.

359
00:18:15,240 --> 00:18:15,800
No.

360
00:18:19,920 --> 00:18:21,440
Hear me out first. I...

361
00:18:22,240 --> 00:18:24,800
My mom wants to apply for permanent residency,

362
00:18:24,800 --> 00:18:25,800
but she needs

363
00:18:25,920 --> 00:18:27,800
your divorce decree from back then.

364
00:18:27,800 --> 00:18:29,280
We each got a copy of the divorce decree.

365
00:18:29,280 --> 00:18:30,880
I tore mine up a long time ago.

366
00:18:32,440 --> 00:18:35,120
Can you just cooperate with her to get a replacement?

367
00:18:35,120 --> 00:18:36,920
I cooperated with her to get a divorce once.

368
00:18:36,920 --> 00:18:37,560
What?

369
00:18:37,560 --> 00:18:39,760
Do I have to cooperate with her to get a second divorce?

370
00:18:39,760 --> 00:18:42,040
It's simple this time. Just sign a paper.

371
00:18:43,880 --> 00:18:46,040
When we divorced, she said we'd never see each other again.

372
00:18:46,040 --> 00:18:47,570
Now she comes to me for help.

373
00:18:48,000 --> 00:18:49,040
I can't do it.

374
00:18:49,200 --> 00:18:49,880
No way.

375
00:18:50,520 --> 00:18:51,200
Okay.

376
00:18:51,760 --> 00:18:53,360
I'm just passing on a message for my mom.

377
00:18:53,360 --> 00:18:54,440
Think about it.

378
00:18:54,920 --> 00:18:57,880
Did you come today just for your mom's business?

379
00:18:58,760 --> 00:19:00,620
Then go back and tell Guo Chunling

380
00:19:00,840 --> 00:19:02,770
that I will never do her this favor.

381
00:19:24,720 --> 00:19:25,520
You're back.

382
00:19:28,800 --> 00:19:29,720
How is Zhao Jia?

383
00:19:30,440 --> 00:19:31,520
Do you even need to ask?

384
00:19:31,520 --> 00:19:32,780
Definitely not great.

385
00:19:33,760 --> 00:19:34,600
Let me ask you,

386
00:19:35,360 --> 00:19:36,280
did you already know

387
00:19:36,280 --> 00:19:38,040
about Cheng Fei's affair?

388
00:19:40,320 --> 00:19:42,280
From a legal perspective, he didn't cheat.

389
00:19:42,280 --> 00:19:43,360
What do you mean?

390
00:19:43,800 --> 00:19:45,860
Emotional cheating isn't cheating?

391
00:19:46,720 --> 00:19:47,560
Actually, if two people

392
00:19:47,560 --> 00:19:49,080
really can't get along,

393
00:19:49,920 --> 00:19:52,800
divorce is the best choice.

394
00:19:53,280 --> 00:19:56,360
Yes, divorce itself isn't the problem.

395
00:19:57,040 --> 00:19:58,440
Isn't the problem now

396
00:19:59,440 --> 00:20:01,600
that Cheng Fei actively betrayed the marriage?

397
00:20:01,600 --> 00:20:03,080
Our current roles

398
00:20:03,080 --> 00:20:04,120
are as their lawyers.

399
00:20:04,120 --> 00:20:06,380
We just need to protect their interests.

400
00:20:06,600 --> 00:20:08,800
Let's not judge their moral standards.

401
00:20:09,600 --> 00:20:10,280
Fine.

402
00:20:10,720 --> 00:20:13,380
Then how about this. Pass a message to Cheng Fei.

403
00:20:13,480 --> 00:20:15,600
Zhao Jia is determined to get the child.

404
00:20:15,600 --> 00:20:17,800
Alright. Pass a message to Zhao Jia too.

405
00:20:18,080 --> 00:20:20,680
Cheng Fei is determined to have this child too.

406
00:20:22,560 --> 00:20:24,000
He is the party at fault.

407
00:20:24,000 --> 00:20:26,040
What right does he have to fight for custody?

408
00:20:26,040 --> 00:20:28,800
Cheating does affect the court's

409
00:20:28,800 --> 00:20:30,360
judgment on marital fault.

410
00:20:30,400 --> 00:20:32,760
However, the custody ruling

411
00:20:33,320 --> 00:20:35,720
is mainly based on the best interests of the child,

412
00:20:35,720 --> 00:20:38,560
not solely on who is at fault in the marriage.

413
00:20:39,480 --> 00:20:41,280
The best interests of the child.

414
00:20:41,280 --> 00:20:43,080
The court will take into account

415
00:20:43,160 --> 00:20:45,000
who can provide a more stable

416
00:20:45,160 --> 00:20:47,000
and healthier living environment for the child.

417
00:20:47,000 --> 00:20:48,520
I raised Nuannuan.

418
00:20:49,800 --> 00:20:52,400
I have done much more for Nuannuan than she has.

419
00:20:53,800 --> 00:20:56,560
She doesn't even have time to spend with Nuannuan.

420
00:20:56,560 --> 00:20:58,820
I don't feel safe leaving her in her care.

421
00:21:00,280 --> 00:21:02,680
Once, she even caused Nuannuan to get hurt.

422
00:21:04,560 --> 00:21:05,760
When did this happen?

423
00:21:07,000 --> 00:21:07,840
I

424
00:21:07,840 --> 00:21:09,840
hate handling divorce cases the most.

425
00:21:09,840 --> 00:21:11,770
When two people first get married,

426
00:21:12,080 --> 00:21:13,960
they are so deeply in love.

427
00:21:14,280 --> 00:21:14,880
But when they divorce,

428
00:21:14,880 --> 00:21:16,810
they want to tear each other apart.

429
00:21:17,840 --> 00:21:19,200
The ugliness of human nature

430
00:21:19,200 --> 00:21:21,040
is fully exposed.

431
00:21:21,440 --> 00:21:24,040
It's one thing for adults to hurt each other,

432
00:21:24,040 --> 00:21:27,300
but in the end, it's often the children who suffer the most.

433
00:21:29,560 --> 00:21:31,680
I went through the bank statements completely

434
00:21:31,680 --> 00:21:33,080
and made a new discovery.

435
00:21:35,400 --> 00:21:36,840
At this time.

436
00:21:38,360 --> 00:21:39,880
Come and look at this.

437
00:21:54,200 --> 00:21:54,600
Cheng.

438
00:21:55,600 --> 00:21:57,330
We found a new piece of evidence

439
00:21:57,560 --> 00:21:59,090
that might be in your favor.

440
00:21:59,640 --> 00:22:00,600
In my favor?

441
00:22:08,160 --> 00:22:09,880
Next, the plaintiff and the defendant

442
00:22:09,880 --> 00:22:13,340
will present and cross-examine evidence regarding custody.

443
00:22:13,640 --> 00:22:14,300
Your Honor,

444
00:22:14,400 --> 00:22:15,080
Exhibit 1.

445
00:22:15,240 --> 00:22:17,520
These are the chat records of my client

446
00:22:17,520 --> 00:22:19,320
in the child's class parent group.

447
00:22:19,320 --> 00:22:21,120
From kindergarten to elementary school,

448
00:22:21,120 --> 00:22:22,240
it was entirely my client

449
00:22:22,240 --> 00:22:23,760
communicating alone,

450
00:22:23,800 --> 00:22:25,640
while the defendant had zero participation.

451
00:22:25,640 --> 00:22:26,400
I disagree.

452
00:22:26,400 --> 00:22:28,480
There is more than one way to participate in education.

453
00:22:28,480 --> 00:22:30,800
Providing financial support is also very important.

454
00:22:30,800 --> 00:22:32,880
Your Honor, these are the receipts

455
00:22:32,880 --> 00:22:35,520
for all the tuition fees paid by my client.

456
00:22:35,600 --> 00:22:36,400
Evidence Two.

457
00:22:36,880 --> 00:22:39,480
This is a photo of the child participating in a piano competition.

458
00:22:39,480 --> 00:22:42,160
My client was also the only one accompanying the child

459
00:22:42,160 --> 00:22:43,280
on such an important day,

460
00:22:43,280 --> 00:22:45,040
while the defendant was absent.

461
00:22:45,040 --> 00:22:46,280
So it can be understood that

462
00:22:46,280 --> 00:22:48,960
the defendant's attention to the child

463
00:22:49,040 --> 00:22:49,960
is insufficient.

464
00:22:49,960 --> 00:22:50,640
I disagree.

465
00:22:50,640 --> 00:22:53,000
These are the receipts for my client's purchase of the piano

466
00:22:53,000 --> 00:22:56,120
and the payment for piano lessons.

467
00:22:56,480 --> 00:22:58,200
If my client hadn't been

468
00:22:58,200 --> 00:22:59,960
working hard to earn money,

469
00:23:00,160 --> 00:23:00,960
I believe

470
00:23:01,480 --> 00:23:03,480
the child wouldn't have had this competition opportunity.

471
00:23:03,480 --> 00:23:05,720
Your Honor, the defendant has been using financial power

472
00:23:05,720 --> 00:23:06,960
to suppress my client.

473
00:23:06,960 --> 00:23:08,760
We just want to use these

474
00:23:08,760 --> 00:23:09,960
to prove one thing.

475
00:23:10,040 --> 00:23:12,800
The child's material foundation and educational level

476
00:23:12,800 --> 00:23:14,960
cannot plummet because of the divorce.

477
00:23:14,960 --> 00:23:17,600
Money can indeed make up for material losses.

478
00:23:17,840 --> 00:23:21,400
But the trust and affection

479
00:23:21,400 --> 00:23:24,060
accumulated through long-term companionship

480
00:23:24,160 --> 00:23:25,600
cannot be bought with money.

481
00:23:25,600 --> 00:23:26,600
Cannot be bought?

482
00:23:26,680 --> 00:23:28,280
What kind of emotion can compare to

483
00:23:28,280 --> 00:23:29,720
a mother's ten months of pregnancy

484
00:23:29,720 --> 00:23:31,400
and love for her child?

485
00:23:31,400 --> 00:23:33,360
I suffered so much to give birth to this child.

486
00:23:33,360 --> 00:23:34,760
What has he contributed?

487
00:23:35,560 --> 00:23:36,800
I'm sorry, Your Honor.

488
00:23:36,800 --> 00:23:39,080
The reason my client is so emotional

489
00:23:39,080 --> 00:23:40,880
is that she experienced dystocia

490
00:23:40,880 --> 00:23:42,010
during childbirth.

491
00:23:42,160 --> 00:23:44,840
The hospital issued two critical condition notices.

492
00:23:44,840 --> 00:23:46,680
She survived in the end,

493
00:23:46,680 --> 00:23:47,440
but

494
00:23:48,240 --> 00:23:49,640
she lost her fertility.

495
00:23:50,400 --> 00:23:53,280
She can only have this one child in her life.

496
00:23:54,720 --> 00:23:57,160
These are the hospital's critical condition notices,

497
00:23:57,160 --> 00:24:00,090
follow-up medical records, and emergency records.

498
00:24:00,280 --> 00:24:04,080
In addition, I would like to ask the court to take into consideration

499
00:24:04,080 --> 00:24:07,320
the plaintiff's admitted extramarital affair.

500
00:24:07,640 --> 00:24:10,760
Although emotional infidelity does not constitute a statutory fault,

501
00:24:10,760 --> 00:24:13,080
But it still violates the duty of loyalty

502
00:24:13,080 --> 00:24:14,080
in a marriage.

503
00:24:14,400 --> 00:24:15,240
Especially considering

504
00:24:15,240 --> 00:24:17,440
that the plaintiff is very likely to remarry, have more children,

505
00:24:17,440 --> 00:24:18,720
and start a new family.

506
00:24:19,080 --> 00:24:20,680
Therefore, we believe

507
00:24:20,680 --> 00:24:24,010
it is more appropriate for the child to stay with the mother.

508
00:24:32,520 --> 00:24:34,280
Two years ago, the child needed to take swimming lessons,

509
00:24:34,280 --> 00:24:36,400
and had to take a shower after class.

510
00:24:36,680 --> 00:24:37,800
And the women's shower room must be entered

511
00:24:37,800 --> 00:24:39,360
with the mother herself.

512
00:24:40,000 --> 00:24:42,680
But after making an appointment,

513
00:24:42,680 --> 00:24:43,800
the defendant failed to show up.

514
00:24:43,800 --> 00:24:45,280
So my client,

515
00:24:45,280 --> 00:24:46,520
having no other choice,

516
00:24:46,520 --> 00:24:49,960
let the child enter the women's shower room alone to wash up.

517
00:24:50,360 --> 00:24:52,720
As a result, an accident occurred during this process,

518
00:24:52,720 --> 00:24:54,320
leading to a fractured hand.

519
00:24:54,360 --> 00:24:56,440
An isolated accident

520
00:24:56,680 --> 00:24:58,200
cannot prove that my client

521
00:24:58,200 --> 00:24:59,720
was negligent.

522
00:24:59,720 --> 00:25:00,160
Your Honor,

523
00:25:00,160 --> 00:25:02,280
may I question the plaintiff directly?

524
00:25:02,280 --> 00:25:02,680
Objection.

525
00:25:02,680 --> 00:25:04,280
Overruled. You may proceed.

526
00:25:08,160 --> 00:25:08,800
Zhao Jia.

527
00:25:10,440 --> 00:25:13,400
Why were you so late that day?

528
00:25:17,680 --> 00:25:19,440
Well, I think

529
00:25:20,720 --> 00:25:22,360
I had an appointment with an out-of-town client,

530
00:25:22,360 --> 00:25:24,680
so I left late.

531
00:25:24,680 --> 00:25:26,160
Then I ran into a huge traffic jam,

532
00:25:26,160 --> 00:25:27,680
and we were discussing business.

533
00:25:27,680 --> 00:25:29,280
Is this out-of-town client

534
00:25:30,440 --> 00:25:31,440
surnamed Huang?

535
00:25:34,200 --> 00:25:34,960
Your Honor,

536
00:25:35,360 --> 00:25:38,400
I would like to submit an additional piece of evidence to the court.

537
00:25:38,400 --> 00:25:39,840
These are the defendant's bank statements.

538
00:25:39,840 --> 00:25:42,440
The date on it is August 4th, two years ago,

539
00:25:42,440 --> 00:25:44,680
which was the Qixi Festival of the year

540
00:25:44,680 --> 00:25:46,200
Nuannuan had the accident.

541
00:25:46,200 --> 00:25:47,000
And on that day,

542
00:25:47,000 --> 00:25:49,440
the defendant received a transfer from a man surnamed Huang

543
00:25:49,440 --> 00:25:52,360
in the amount of 1,314.

544
00:25:52,360 --> 00:25:54,520
I believe everyone understands

545
00:25:54,520 --> 00:25:55,600
the special meaning of this amount.

546
00:25:55,600 --> 00:25:56,680
And this man surnamed Huang

547
00:25:56,680 --> 00:25:59,720
did not just have a simple working relationship with the defendant.

548
00:25:59,720 --> 00:26:02,440
The defendant met this man two years ago

549
00:26:02,440 --> 00:26:04,440
and had an extramarital affair with him.

550
00:26:04,440 --> 00:26:06,600
And on the very day Nuannuan had the accident,

551
00:26:06,600 --> 00:26:09,400
it was because the two were on a date and lost track of time

552
00:26:09,400 --> 00:26:11,440
that the child had an accident.

553
00:26:11,440 --> 00:26:13,160
It's not like that.

554
00:26:13,160 --> 00:26:14,680
The hotel records are right there.

555
00:26:14,680 --> 00:26:15,720
Do you want to see them?

556
00:26:15,720 --> 00:26:16,960
Those... that...

557
00:26:17,080 --> 00:26:18,960
That day I was actually trying to...

558
00:26:18,960 --> 00:26:20,640
You still won't admit it even now.

559
00:26:20,640 --> 00:26:23,040
Plaintiff, please control your emotions.

560
00:26:23,120 --> 00:26:25,760
Given the facts ascertained by the court so far,

561
00:26:25,760 --> 00:26:28,120
Since the child is over eight years old,

562
00:26:28,360 --> 00:26:31,360
this court needs to seek the child's true wishes.

563
00:26:31,600 --> 00:26:33,480
After the plaintiff and defendant go back,

564
00:26:33,480 --> 00:26:35,920
please comfort the child psychologically.

565
00:26:35,920 --> 00:26:38,720
The court will notify you of the next hearing time.

566
00:26:39,120 --> 00:26:40,120
Court adjourned.

567
00:26:46,360 --> 00:26:47,000
Long.

568
00:26:47,680 --> 00:26:48,520
I'm sorry.

569
00:26:48,960 --> 00:26:51,360
I didn't mean to hide this from you.

570
00:26:51,440 --> 00:26:52,520
It's just that

571
00:26:53,280 --> 00:26:54,520
I couldn't say it.

572
00:26:54,520 --> 00:26:56,320
Zhao Jia, you didn't let me down.

573
00:26:56,360 --> 00:26:57,960
You let yourself down.

574
00:26:58,520 --> 00:26:59,720
By hiding this,

575
00:27:00,960 --> 00:27:03,020
you put us in such a passive position.

576
00:27:04,920 --> 00:27:07,520
I was under so much pressure at that time,

577
00:27:07,520 --> 00:27:09,520
and I had no way to relieve it.

578
00:27:09,600 --> 00:27:10,440
So I

579
00:27:11,080 --> 00:27:12,760
wanted to talk to Cheng Fei

580
00:27:12,760 --> 00:27:14,200
and let him listen to me.

581
00:27:14,200 --> 00:27:15,520
But before I could say a few words,

582
00:27:15,520 --> 00:27:17,160
he told me to change jobs.

583
00:27:17,160 --> 00:27:18,160
You know?

584
00:27:18,160 --> 00:27:20,160
He didn't want to understand me.

585
00:27:20,520 --> 00:27:23,720
I was confused for a moment,

586
00:27:24,000 --> 00:27:26,200
but I quickly cut off that relationship.

587
00:27:26,200 --> 00:27:26,720
That day,

588
00:27:26,720 --> 00:27:29,680
I was actually going to make it clear to that person.

589
00:27:30,280 --> 00:27:33,800
I didn't expect Nuannuan to have an accident.

590
00:27:34,680 --> 00:27:36,440
I regret it. I really...

591
00:27:37,440 --> 00:27:38,960
I really regret it.

592
00:27:40,880 --> 00:27:41,520
Long.

593
00:27:41,640 --> 00:27:43,400
That's all of it.

594
00:27:43,400 --> 00:27:45,530
I'm not hiding anything else from you.

595
00:27:45,920 --> 00:27:47,440
Please help me.

596
00:27:47,440 --> 00:27:49,440
I can give up the marriage,

597
00:27:50,880 --> 00:27:52,760
but I can't lose Nuannuan.

598
00:28:11,200 --> 00:28:11,960
Mom.

599
00:28:13,120 --> 00:28:15,450
Nuannuan, go inside and do your homework.

600
00:28:37,160 --> 00:28:38,760
What did you say to the child?

601
00:28:42,120 --> 00:28:42,760
I'm asking you a question.

602
00:28:42,760 --> 00:28:44,440
What did you say to the child?

603
00:28:47,240 --> 00:28:48,000
I'm warning you.

604
00:28:48,000 --> 00:28:49,860
Don't talk nonsense to the child.

605
00:28:50,000 --> 00:28:50,860
Did you hear me?

606
00:28:52,840 --> 00:28:53,400
Did you hear me?

607
00:28:53,400 --> 00:28:54,460
I'm talking to you.

608
00:28:56,840 --> 00:28:57,520
What do you mean?

609
00:28:57,520 --> 00:28:58,680
I'm talking to you.

610
00:29:34,440 --> 00:29:34,960
Son.

611
00:29:35,000 --> 00:29:37,320
Why didn't you answer when I called you so many times?

612
00:29:37,320 --> 00:29:39,360
The agent urged me today.

613
00:29:39,440 --> 00:29:40,770
What did Li Guochen say?

614
00:29:40,840 --> 00:29:41,560
My dad said

615
00:29:42,040 --> 00:29:42,680
he'll think about it.

616
00:29:42,680 --> 00:29:43,540
Think about it?

617
00:29:44,120 --> 00:29:45,320
Ridiculous.

618
00:29:45,320 --> 00:29:46,560
It's just signing a paper.

619
00:29:46,560 --> 00:29:48,240
It's neither against the rules nor illegal.

620
00:29:48,240 --> 00:29:50,080
What is there to think about?

621
00:29:51,720 --> 00:29:54,480
Does he think I should beg him?

622
00:29:55,760 --> 00:29:57,090
I have to take this call.

623
00:29:57,120 --> 00:29:57,800
No, you...

624
00:30:02,160 --> 00:30:02,760
Cheng Fei.

625
00:30:02,760 --> 00:30:04,800
Can you pick up Nuannuan tomorrow?

626
00:30:05,000 --> 00:30:06,320
Ask her what she wants.

627
00:30:07,240 --> 00:30:08,840
I'll talk to her teacher.

628
00:30:23,160 --> 00:30:24,280
What a coincidence.

629
00:30:24,280 --> 00:30:25,160
Zhao Jia didn't come?

630
00:30:25,160 --> 00:30:27,120
What about Cheng Fei? He didn't come either?

631
00:30:27,120 --> 00:30:27,720
No.

632
00:30:27,880 --> 00:30:29,280
They are quite in sync.

633
00:30:31,960 --> 00:30:32,800
Jindou.

634
00:30:34,200 --> 00:30:35,040
Nuannuan.

635
00:30:35,240 --> 00:30:35,960
Nuannuan.

636
00:30:36,120 --> 00:30:37,400
Aunt, Uncle.

637
00:30:37,600 --> 00:30:38,760
Mom and Dad are busy today.

638
00:30:38,760 --> 00:30:40,890
So we're picking you up. Are you happy?

639
00:30:43,840 --> 00:30:44,800
Thank you, teacher.

640
00:30:44,800 --> 00:30:45,640
No problem.

641
00:30:45,640 --> 00:30:46,760
I'll leave her to you then.

642
00:30:46,760 --> 00:30:47,490
Don't worry.

643
00:30:55,800 --> 00:30:57,120
What's wrong, Nuannuan?

644
00:30:57,120 --> 00:30:59,160
Are you not feeling well,

645
00:30:59,440 --> 00:31:01,520
or is the food not good?

646
00:31:03,800 --> 00:31:04,680
Then what is it?

647
00:31:08,400 --> 00:31:10,730
Will you guys always pick me up from now on?

648
00:31:14,160 --> 00:31:15,320
Of course not.

649
00:31:16,240 --> 00:31:18,960
Mom and Dad are just busy today.

650
00:31:18,960 --> 00:31:21,800
So they sent us to pick you up.

651
00:31:23,120 --> 00:31:24,280
Are my mom and dad

652
00:31:25,760 --> 00:31:27,320
getting a divorce?

653
00:31:37,920 --> 00:31:39,960
Why would you ask that, Nuannuan?

654
00:31:41,400 --> 00:31:43,040
I heard them arguing.

655
00:31:43,520 --> 00:31:46,050
And they don't sleep in the same room anymore.

656
00:31:46,440 --> 00:31:47,920
Nuannuan is growing up.

657
00:31:48,480 --> 00:31:50,410
Worrying about Mom and Dad, right?

658
00:31:52,200 --> 00:31:55,760
Is there any way to make them make up?

659
00:32:05,760 --> 00:32:08,440
This isn't something a kid should worry about.

660
00:32:09,160 --> 00:32:11,420
What a kid should worry about right now is

661
00:32:12,200 --> 00:32:13,480
whether you've finished your homework,

662
00:32:13,480 --> 00:32:13,960
right?

663
00:32:13,960 --> 00:32:15,160
Have you finished it?

664
00:32:16,120 --> 00:32:16,920
Not yet.

665
00:32:17,520 --> 00:32:18,560
Take it out and test me.

666
00:32:18,560 --> 00:32:20,120
Let's see if I can do it.

667
00:32:34,200 --> 00:32:36,930
Nuannuan is learning such difficult things now.

668
00:32:38,400 --> 00:32:39,680
I can't even do it.

669
00:32:46,120 --> 00:32:46,720
Come here.

670
00:32:48,040 --> 00:32:49,800
Nuannuan did her homework very well.

671
00:32:49,800 --> 00:32:51,720
Okay, say goodbye to your aunt.

672
00:32:51,800 --> 00:32:52,440
Bye-bye.

673
00:32:52,440 --> 00:32:53,520
And your uncle.

674
00:32:53,720 --> 00:32:54,480
Bye-bye.

675
00:32:58,440 --> 00:32:59,480
Nuannuan is back.

676
00:33:00,440 --> 00:33:01,560
It's time for your milk.

677
00:33:01,560 --> 00:33:02,720
Drink your milk.

678
00:33:02,720 --> 00:33:05,000
Didn't you just say you wanted orange juice?

679
00:33:05,000 --> 00:33:06,640
Mom will pour you some orange juice.

680
00:33:06,640 --> 00:33:07,480
Orange juice is too sweet.

681
00:33:07,480 --> 00:33:08,440
It's bad for your teeth.

682
00:33:08,440 --> 00:33:10,440
It's okay to drink it once in a while.

683
00:33:10,440 --> 00:33:12,000
Isn't that right, Nuannuan?

684
00:33:12,000 --> 00:33:13,760
We drink milk to grow tall.

685
00:33:15,160 --> 00:33:16,640
Mom just bought the orange juice today.

686
00:33:16,640 --> 00:33:18,080
Look, it's still cold.

687
00:33:18,080 --> 00:33:19,080
It's so hot today.

688
00:33:19,080 --> 00:33:20,540
Let's drink orange juice.

689
00:33:27,560 --> 00:33:29,360
When Nuannuan asked me just now,

690
00:33:30,040 --> 00:33:32,280
I really didn't know how to answer her.

691
00:33:32,520 --> 00:33:35,000
If I lied to her,

692
00:33:35,080 --> 00:33:36,720
that definitely wouldn't work.

693
00:33:36,720 --> 00:33:37,720
But I also felt

694
00:33:39,000 --> 00:33:41,060
I couldn't tell her the truth either.

695
00:33:42,040 --> 00:33:43,720
You know, when adults make mistakes

696
00:33:43,720 --> 00:33:46,450
and let such a young child bear the consequences,

697
00:33:46,520 --> 00:33:47,640
it's really cruel.

698
00:33:49,480 --> 00:33:51,610
Because a child's world is very small,

699
00:33:51,960 --> 00:33:52,960
so small

700
00:33:53,920 --> 00:33:55,920
that it can only hold their parents.

701
00:34:08,960 --> 00:34:09,800
Drink slowly.

702
00:34:15,040 --> 00:34:16,900
If you don't want to drink, don't.

703
00:34:34,080 --> 00:34:34,800
Nuannuan,

704
00:34:35,520 --> 00:34:36,520
I don't feel well.

705
00:34:53,239 --> 00:34:54,320
If you don't do live streaming,

706
00:34:54,320 --> 00:34:55,159
if you don't use the internet,

707
00:34:55,159 --> 00:34:56,440
you have no idea

708
00:34:56,440 --> 00:34:58,000
how many tricks there are

709
00:34:58,000 --> 00:34:59,080
in live streaming.

710
00:34:59,080 --> 00:35:01,520
Which of the things you do doesn't have a lot of tricks?

711
00:35:01,520 --> 00:35:02,160
Don't interrupt me.

712
00:35:02,160 --> 00:35:03,240
Let me finish.

713
00:35:04,040 --> 00:35:06,680
You have to build a persona for live streaming.

714
00:35:06,680 --> 00:35:09,800
What about your persona as a misguided old man?

715
00:35:09,920 --> 00:35:11,320
Isn't it natural? Do you still need to build it?

716
00:35:11,320 --> 00:35:13,080
What misguided old man?

717
00:35:13,320 --> 00:35:14,680
You haven't been to my live stream.

718
00:35:14,680 --> 00:35:16,240
I have so many fans.

719
00:35:16,800 --> 00:35:18,660
Why don't you open an account too?

720
00:35:18,800 --> 00:35:19,480
We can do a PK,

721
00:35:19,480 --> 00:35:20,440
and then we can gain fans for each other.

722
00:35:20,440 --> 00:35:21,040
You know?

723
00:35:21,120 --> 00:35:22,200
What would I interact with you about?

724
00:35:22,200 --> 00:35:23,240
Reenacting across the screen

725
00:35:23,240 --> 00:35:24,800
how I caught you back then?

726
00:35:25,240 --> 00:35:27,000
What's wrong with you?

727
00:35:28,000 --> 00:35:29,680
Since I walked into your house today,

728
00:35:29,680 --> 00:35:31,000
you've been attacking me

729
00:35:31,000 --> 00:35:31,960
with every few words.

730
00:35:31,960 --> 00:35:32,800
When did I attack you?

731
00:35:32,800 --> 00:35:34,160
I'm just upset.

732
00:35:34,800 --> 00:35:35,800
What are you upset about?

733
00:35:35,800 --> 00:35:36,800
The kids?

734
00:35:36,800 --> 00:35:38,320
What kids? Recently...

735
00:35:40,560 --> 00:35:41,640
The letter... the letter came back.

736
00:35:41,640 --> 00:35:42,700
Don't go. Don't go.

737
00:35:43,360 --> 00:35:44,420
What are you doing?

738
00:35:44,960 --> 00:35:47,160
Coming. My son is back.

739
00:35:50,840 --> 00:35:51,680
Chunling.

740
00:35:53,000 --> 00:35:54,080
Sorry.

741
00:35:54,840 --> 00:35:57,680
My name is Jennifer now.

742
00:36:00,840 --> 00:36:01,720
Jenni. Jenni.

743
00:36:03,560 --> 00:36:04,680
Please excuse us.

744
00:36:05,440 --> 00:36:07,800
I have private matters to discuss with him.

745
00:36:07,800 --> 00:36:08,640
Okay. Okay.

746
00:36:10,400 --> 00:36:12,330
I finally know why you're so upset.

747
00:36:12,480 --> 00:36:14,760
Okay, I'm leaving now, Jennifer.

748
00:36:23,800 --> 00:36:25,480
Why does my dad keep looking for you?

749
00:36:25,480 --> 00:36:26,640
He likes me.

750
00:36:28,800 --> 00:36:29,360
Godfather.

751
00:36:29,360 --> 00:36:30,080
Xin.

752
00:36:34,320 --> 00:36:36,040
I know you don't want to see me.

753
00:36:36,440 --> 00:36:38,040
I don't want to see you either.

754
00:36:38,040 --> 00:36:39,320
Then why are you here?

755
00:36:39,960 --> 00:36:41,490
Didn't you force me to come?

756
00:36:41,720 --> 00:36:42,680
Doing this

757
00:36:42,840 --> 00:36:44,680
makes it so hard for our son, caught in the middle.

758
00:36:44,680 --> 00:36:46,360
If our son is having a hard time,

759
00:36:46,360 --> 00:36:47,690
isn't it all your doing?

760
00:36:51,520 --> 00:36:52,160
Yes.

761
00:36:53,000 --> 00:36:54,320
This is my business.

762
00:36:54,960 --> 00:36:57,440
Then come to the court with me and sign the papers.

763
00:36:57,440 --> 00:36:58,440
From now on,

764
00:36:58,440 --> 00:37:00,440
I won't disturb your life, Deputy Director Li,

765
00:37:00,440 --> 00:37:01,680
and let you enjoy your old age in peace.

766
00:37:01,680 --> 00:37:02,440
I can't go.

767
00:37:02,440 --> 00:37:03,760
It's such a small thing.

768
00:37:03,760 --> 00:37:05,680
Why are you so selfish?

769
00:37:05,680 --> 00:37:06,560
Am I selfish?

770
00:37:06,560 --> 00:37:07,440
Selfish.

771
00:37:07,480 --> 00:37:09,160
So selfish you don't care about your family.

772
00:37:09,160 --> 00:37:10,160
After all these years,

773
00:37:10,160 --> 00:37:11,640
why haven't you changed at all?

774
00:37:11,640 --> 00:37:13,240
You haven't changed either.

775
00:37:13,320 --> 00:37:14,680
Still as aggressive as ever.

776
00:37:14,680 --> 00:37:15,920
Am I wrong?

777
00:37:16,040 --> 00:37:18,560
In the past, I asked you to do some business,

778
00:37:19,040 --> 00:37:19,840
but you absolutely refused.

779
00:37:19,840 --> 00:37:20,960
When asked why,

780
00:37:21,000 --> 00:37:22,480
you couldn't say a word.

781
00:37:22,680 --> 00:37:23,200
And you would often

782
00:37:23,200 --> 00:37:24,480
disappear from home for days.

783
00:37:24,480 --> 00:37:25,740
Enough, Guo Chunling.

784
00:37:25,960 --> 00:37:27,200
Stop bringing up the past.

785
00:37:27,200 --> 00:37:29,160
So what if I bring up the past?

786
00:37:29,160 --> 00:37:30,560
Look at you now,

787
00:37:30,560 --> 00:37:31,480
still living in this

788
00:37:31,480 --> 00:37:33,360
hexagonal room.

789
00:37:33,360 --> 00:37:34,960
Good thing I divorced you early.

790
00:37:34,960 --> 00:37:36,200
You just love money

791
00:37:36,200 --> 00:37:37,360
and vanity.

792
00:37:37,360 --> 00:37:39,160
Look how you led your son astray.

793
00:37:39,160 --> 00:37:41,480
Otherwise, would he be so distant from me now?

794
00:37:41,480 --> 00:37:42,680
That's because you didn't fulfill

795
00:37:42,680 --> 00:37:44,040
your responsibilities as a father.

796
00:37:44,040 --> 00:37:44,840
Did you?

797
00:37:44,840 --> 00:37:46,040
Of course I did.

798
00:37:46,320 --> 00:37:48,850
If I hadn't divorced you, my son would be dead.

799
00:37:53,320 --> 00:37:54,920
Did I want to harm my son?

800
00:37:54,920 --> 00:37:56,440
Think about what you did.

801
00:37:56,560 --> 00:37:57,400
You went abroad,

802
00:37:57,400 --> 00:37:58,600
started a new family,

803
00:37:58,640 --> 00:38:00,240
and left him alone back home.

804
00:38:00,440 --> 00:38:02,080
Li Guochen, how dare you accuse me?

805
00:38:02,080 --> 00:38:03,360
Don't point your finger at me.

806
00:38:03,360 --> 00:38:04,200
So what if I do?

807
00:38:04,200 --> 00:38:05,160
Are you trying to assault a police officer?

808
00:38:05,160 --> 00:38:06,480
Assault a police officer? So what if I assault you?

809
00:38:06,480 --> 00:38:06,920
Don't touch me.

810
00:38:06,920 --> 00:38:07,560
I'll touch you.

811
00:38:07,560 --> 00:38:08,480
What can you do to me?

812
00:38:08,480 --> 00:38:09,560
Arrest me?

813
00:38:30,320 --> 00:38:31,960
Why are you arguing again?

814
00:38:33,880 --> 00:38:35,520
I heard you from outside.

815
00:38:37,000 --> 00:38:38,320
Just like old times.

816
00:38:40,480 --> 00:38:41,480
You two

817
00:38:43,200 --> 00:38:45,200
always just stick to your own views

818
00:38:45,800 --> 00:38:47,330
and fight to the bitter end.

819
00:38:47,960 --> 00:38:49,690
You both say it's for my own good

820
00:38:50,200 --> 00:38:52,130
and that you're looking out for me.

821
00:38:52,520 --> 00:38:54,120
But what I really want

822
00:38:55,640 --> 00:38:56,900
and what I'm thinking,

823
00:38:59,000 --> 00:39:00,680
you've never cared about.

824
00:39:04,520 --> 00:39:06,120
Enough. I'm grown up now.

825
00:39:07,200 --> 00:39:08,200
Stop arguing.

826
00:39:11,200 --> 00:39:13,200
It's not easy for us to get together.

827
00:39:13,680 --> 00:39:16,480
Even though you two are no longer husband and wife,

828
00:39:17,320 --> 00:39:18,680
one is still my dad,

829
00:39:20,000 --> 00:39:21,600
and the other is still my mom.

830
00:39:49,160 --> 00:39:50,220
Throw the gun over,

831
00:39:50,240 --> 00:39:51,200
or I'll kill him.

832
00:39:53,200 --> 00:39:54,040
Listen to me.

833
00:39:55,120 --> 00:39:56,000
Let him go first

834
00:39:57,200 --> 00:39:58,000
and try to get leniency.

835
00:39:58,000 --> 00:39:59,040
Give me the gun.

836
00:39:59,320 --> 00:40:00,640
Is your gun more important,

837
00:40:00,640 --> 00:40:02,000
or is your son more important?

838
00:40:02,000 --> 00:40:02,680
You choose.

839
00:40:03,680 --> 00:40:04,600
Dad.

840
00:40:08,600 --> 00:40:09,480
Dad.

841
00:40:25,960 --> 00:40:30,120
Son, son.

842
00:40:30,640 --> 00:40:31,960
Son.

843
00:40:33,360 --> 00:40:34,920
Son.

844
00:40:39,000 --> 00:40:39,760
Divorce.

845
00:40:40,120 --> 00:40:41,320
Sign it right now.

846
00:40:42,000 --> 00:40:44,920
Chunling, this was really an accident.

847
00:40:44,920 --> 00:40:45,650
An accident?

848
00:40:46,680 --> 00:40:48,000
Look at our son.

849
00:40:48,000 --> 00:40:49,480
You almost killed him.

850
00:40:49,680 --> 00:40:50,680
I promise you.

851
00:40:51,480 --> 00:40:53,000
This will never happen again.

852
00:40:53,000 --> 00:40:54,130
How can you promise?

853
00:40:54,320 --> 00:40:55,680
You value this uniform

854
00:40:55,920 --> 00:40:57,880
more than your son's life.

855
00:41:00,960 --> 00:41:03,040
Li Guochen, say no more.

856
00:41:04,480 --> 00:41:05,610
Let's get a divorce.

857
00:41:06,120 --> 00:41:06,680
Fine.

858
00:41:07,000 --> 00:41:07,920
You can leave,

859
00:41:08,000 --> 00:41:09,260
but Xiaoxin must stay.

860
00:41:09,280 --> 00:41:12,000
Impossible. My son stays with me.

861
00:41:12,000 --> 00:41:12,800
Guo Chunling.

862
00:41:14,400 --> 00:41:15,280
I don't agree.

863
00:41:15,880 --> 00:41:16,520
Fine.

864
00:41:18,520 --> 00:41:20,580
Then let's see how the court decides.

865
00:41:51,080 --> 00:41:52,600
Plaintiff.

866
00:41:52,600 --> 00:41:53,400
Little boy,

867
00:41:53,480 --> 00:41:55,400
would you rather live with your dad

868
00:41:55,400 --> 00:41:57,400
or your mom?

869
00:42:38,160 --> 00:42:38,880
Here, here.

870
00:42:38,880 --> 00:42:39,880
Mom is here. Come.

871
00:42:40,560 --> 00:42:42,200
Here. Let's go.

872
00:42:46,280 --> 00:42:47,800
Oh my God, slow down.

873
00:42:47,960 --> 00:42:48,520
Okay, okay.

874
00:42:48,520 --> 00:42:50,080
Let's go. Alright.

875
00:42:51,120 --> 00:42:51,880
Miss.

876
00:42:52,360 --> 00:42:54,600
Where is Nuannuan? Hasn't she come out yet?

877
00:42:54,600 --> 00:42:55,480
In the afternoon,

878
00:42:55,480 --> 00:42:57,680
Nuannuan's father picked her up early.

879
00:42:57,680 --> 00:42:58,880
Didn't he tell you?
